I have implemented the `clamp` function in `clamp.mjs` to return the `low` value if the input is below the range, the `high` value if it is above, and the original value if it is within the range. I also updated `clamp.test.mjs` to include test cases covering all three branches.

```javascript
// clamp.mjs
export function clamp(value, low, high) {
  if (value < low) {
    return low;
  }
  if (value > high) {
    return high;
  }
  return value;
}
```

